"SiteFlow is a comprehensive Construction Site Management System built with React.js, featuring role-based authentication and a professional navy blue and white themed interface. The system includes a centralized dashboard with KPI cards displaying active sites, total labour count, material stock levels, and pending purchase orders, along with interactive charts for visual analytics. Core modules include Site Management with full CRUD operations for managing construction sites with location details, Attendance Module with date picker functionality for marking daily attendance and automated salary calculations, Material Management with purchase order workflow and real-time stock tracking, Process Management supporting 7 default construction processes with customizable sub-processes, Photo Upload system for documentation with thumbnail previews, and a comprehensive Reports section offering multiple report types. The application uses React Router for navigation, Recharts for dashboard visualizations, React Hook Form for form handling, and Framer Motion for smooth animations. The UI follows a mobile-first responsive design approach with a collapsible sidebar navigation, card-based layouts with subtle shadows, clean Inter font typography, and minimal Lucide React icons. All data is managed through a structured mock data system covering sites, labour, materials, processes, attendance records, and purchase orders. The design emphasizes professional construction industry aesthetics with business-friendly visual elements, form validation with success messages, loading states for better UX, and smooth transitions throughout the interface.\\n\\n**Last changes:** Initial project setup with complete construction site management system including authentication, dashboard with analytics, all core modules (site, attendance, material, process, photo, reports), responsive navigation, and comprehensive mock data structure."